<h3><% __('Toronto Agreement') |h %></h3>

<h4><% __('Rapid prepublication data release should be encouraged for projects with the following attributes:') |h %></h4>

<ul>
<li><% __('Large scale (requiring significant resources over time)') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Broad utility') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Creating reference data sets') |h %></li>

<li><% __('Associated with community buy-in') |h %></li>
</ul>

<h4><% __('Funding agencies should facilitate the specification of data-release policies for relevant projects by:') |h %></h4>

<ul>
<li><% __('Explicitly informing applicants of data-release requirements, especially mandatory prepublication data release') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Ensuring that evaluation of data release plans is part of the peer-review process') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Proactively establishing analysis plans and timelines for projects releasing data prepublication') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Fostering investigator-initiated prepublication data release') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Helping to develop appropriate consent, security, access and governance mechanisms that protect research participants while encouraging prepublication data release') |h %></li>

<li><% __('Providing long-term support of databases') |h %></li>
</ul>

<h4><% __('Data producers should state their intentions and enable analyses of their data by:') |h %></h4>

<ul>
<li><% __('Informing data users about the data being generated, data standards and quality, planned analyses, timelines, and relevant contact information, ideally through publication of a citable marker paper near the start of the project or by provision of a citable URL at the project or funding-agency website') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Providing relevant metadata (e.g., questionnaires, phenotypes, environmental conditions, and laboratory methods) that will assist other researchers in reproducing and/or independently analysing the data, while protecting interests of individuals enrolled in studies focusing on humans') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Ensuring that research participants are informed that their data will be shared with other scientists in the research community') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Publishing their initial global analyses, as stated in the marker paper or citable URL, in a timely fashion') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Creating databases designed to archive all data (including underlying raw data) in an easily retrievable form and facilitate usage of both pre-processed and processed data') |h %></li>

</ul>

<h4><% __('Data analysts/users should freely analyse released prepublication data and act responsibly in publishing analyses of those data by:') |h %></h4>

<ul>
<li><% __('Respecting the scientific etiquette that allows data producers to publish the first global analyses of their data set') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Reading the citeable document associated with the project') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Accurately and completely citing the source of prepublication data, including the version of the data set (if appropriate)') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Being aware that released prepublication data may be associated with quality issues that will be later rectified by the data producers') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Contacting the data producers to discuss publication plans in the case of overlap between planned analyses') |h %></li>
<li><% __('Ensuring that use of data does not harm research participants and is in conformity with ethical approvals') |h %></li>

<li><% __('Scientific journal editors should engage the research community about issues related to prepublication data release and provide guidance to authors and reviewers on the third-party use of prepublication data in manuscripts') |h %></li>
</ul>


</td></tr></table>
